---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does AnyBucket work with MinIO, Garage and RustFS?',
    a: 'Yes. AnyBucket is a GUI for AWS S3 and any S3-compatible object store — point a connection at your MinIO, Garage or RustFS endpoint and enable path-style addressing if your server needs it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which platforms does the desktop app support?',
    a: 'Windows 10 & 11 (x64, also via WinGet), macOS on Apple Silicon, and Linux (x64 AppImage and .deb). The self-hosted Docker image runs on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a web version I can self-host?',
    a: 'Yes. The same UI runs as a self-hosted S3 web interface in a single Docker container, with all S3 operations performed server-side. It has no built-in auth, so run it behind a reverse proxy that provides authentication and TLS.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where are my S3 access keys stored?',
    a: 'In the desktop app, secret keys live in your OS keychain. In the self-hosted web app, they are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest under a master key you provide.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I prevent accidental deletes?',
    a: 'Each connection has an access mode — read-only, read-write, or read-write-delete — enforced in the Rust backend, not just hidden in the UI.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is AnyBucket free?',
    a: 'Yes. AnyBucket is free and open source under the MIT License.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-night-800 py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
    <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-3">
      {faqs.map((f) => (
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-night-700 bg-night-900 px-5 py-4 open:bg-night-850">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <h3>{f.q}</h3>
            <Icon
              name="heroicons:chevron-down-20-solid"
              width="20"
              height="20"
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="shrink-0 text-ink-faint transition group-open:rotate-180"
            />
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
